  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nBees are very important for the food we eat. When a bee goes from flower to flower to collect nectar, it carries pollen that helps plants make fruits and seeds. About one third of the food crops in the world depend on bees and other pollinators. In the past few decades, bee populations have gone down a lot because of pesticides, disease, and the loss of wild flowers. If bees keep disappearing, foods like apples, almonds, and blueberries could become much harder to grow. People can help by planting flowers and avoiding chemicals in their gardens.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nIn the past few decades, bee populations have gone down a lot because of pesticides, disease, and the loss of wild flowers.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text that say the same thing in fewer words. Keep every fact, name, number and quotation, and keep the claim exactly as strong or as uncertain as it is. Put the best options first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
